{"title":"2010 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 20","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A geometric sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/0/cb07e848f9188a9fd706d99ab6513a7d949c48a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a_n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"35\" height=\"20\" /> has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/f/82fd25d7548dfa831a4133fc927ed7a66500cf28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1=\\sin x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"76\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/0/f800cf6893f0827d2a3d5372d0229438cc65e948.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2=\\cos x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"78\" height=\"10\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/6/8c63f6de716a41cb0b10c644f4d96a19a3ae64fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_3= \\tan x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"80\" height=\"14\" /> for some real number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. For what value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> does <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/5/b35bbbe898fc95d012b6a08532516a8485c6d92d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n=1+\\cos x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"111\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/e/ccefe446ac26b1d2ff26fd59aaaea8ce281b5a83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 4 \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 5 \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 6 \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 7 \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"348\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By the defintion of a geometric sequence, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/7/ef7e140e61e7f2c02a7dee7f2e29951b0de5b737.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos^2x=\\sin x \\tan x$\" width=\"147\" height=\"15\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/1/aa13e9b66ffef6a37a9be3fa57e0a606a5e9454d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan x=\\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"108\" height=\"39\" />, we can rewrite this as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/1/ca1c361e1368dbc1c5a12bb4f290621fac88cde5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos^3x=\\sin^2x$\" width=\"112\" height=\"15\" />. \n</p><p>The common ratio of the sequence is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/8/dd83a266176775fae7bf2f4851ea819387da970e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\cos x}{\\sin x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"40\" height=\"33\" />, so we can write\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/a/1aabb1dd85adb650024782c4a00d25af69ce9d08.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_1= \\sin x\\]\" width=\"76\" height=\"15\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/c/43ca1cff036216ab2bfd7f46fbdb3e5c9fd953cd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_2= \\cos x\\]\" width=\"78\" height=\"11\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/3/b2393d9ecc7f124d48e1f02f9b4e73260bff9d5a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_3= \\frac{\\cos^2x}{\\sin x}\\]\" width=\"88\" height=\"39\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/2/192747714a5472598036838a6af4ca461a7fb764.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_4=\\frac{\\cos^3x}{\\sin^2x}=1\\]\" width=\"122\" height=\"40\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/3/203672b722b8e4a64a0f72c6e2271938abe92355.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_5=\\frac{\\cos x}{\\sin x}\\]\" width=\"80\" height=\"32\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/0/6105eae8dce61679696242306072701b1a158834.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_6=\\frac{\\cos^2x}{\\sin^2x}\\]\" width=\"88\" height=\"40\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/f/9af8c8f10513413e48d001ab1bc43bac716fb4f9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_7=\\frac{\\cos^3x}{\\sin^3x}=\\frac{1}{\\sin x}\\]\" width=\"152\" height=\"40\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/f/67fb2736c525445714ed24588d8b56676298dc00.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_8=\\frac{\\cos x}{\\sin^2 x}=\\frac{1}{\\cos^2 x}\\]\" width=\"159\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><br />\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/3/9f324cfd4df5fa892a1833b2b02d9291073b1a4d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos^3x=\\sin^2x=1-\\cos^2x$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"213\" height=\"16\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/6/c5638f9de83638d59f75341c42b16ec4a171b25f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos^3x+\\cos^2x=1 \\implies \\cos^2x(\\cos x+1)=1 \\implies \\cos x+1=\\frac{1}{\\cos^2 x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"547\" height=\"37\" />, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/a/7ead075983f8dbfa721f00c28be967778b4a6677.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> , making our answer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/f/8afb5aed613a30f7d0dce32866e464fc9181b32e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8 \\Rightarrow \\boxed{E}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"63\" height=\"24\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Notice that the common ratio is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/a/ada2c0a60be10804ac1bca9b527e5979e66a520d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r=\\frac{\\cos(x)}{\\sin(x)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"88\" height=\"45\" />; multiplying it to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/8/9588b40a54c466065cc319ee67b576ed8acc11ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan(x)=\\frac{\\sin(x)}{\\cos(x)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"126\" height=\"43\" /> gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/0/fe0c40815344128c5f5388d25a985a6f16f668e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_4=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"49\" height=\"14\" />. Then, working backwards we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/e/e1e0d718d188a331bc44a7dd69d60eadc898927c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_3=\\frac{1}{r}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"53\" height=\"37\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/f/c2fc05b934387d161a4867774f18ba10fb448350.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2=\\frac{1}{r^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"60\" height=\"37\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/7/0f7eafc6d17912c704ffae773acccd07dda1b8c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1=\\frac{1}{r^3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"60\" height=\"37\" />. Now notice that since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/f/e9f28a0b480bde17dc5f20a933ed7da92802d66e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1=\\sin(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"86\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/7/6477cc49cd88ec6c6294cf93575b17aed2a9e3dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2=\\cos(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"88\" height=\"18\" />, we need <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/e/45e1d434d7048340cddca16498439644d72e64d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1^2+a_2^2=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"88\" height=\"19\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/e/53e1af7c7f68b5aabe486ac2e7e15b66d2299d45.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{r^6}+\\frac{1}{r^4}=\\frac{r^2+1}{r^6}=1\\implies r^2+1=r^6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"307\" height=\"39\" />. Dividing both sides by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/2/e2221c84f16a3f75ae07e5023384cc40d9c05357.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r^2$\" width=\"14\" height=\"15\" /> gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/e/b6e2155a7ff636048fc6e3c63470e3c01d4703e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+\\frac{1}{r^2}=r^4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"91\" height=\"37\" />, which the left side is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/f/f2f54ffd339957d807ce07961aae1f97f0169b51.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+\\cos(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"78\" height=\"18\" />; we see as well that the right hand side is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/a/7ead075983f8dbfa721f00c28be967778b4a6677.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> given <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/0/fe0c40815344128c5f5388d25a985a6f16f668e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_4=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"49\" height=\"14\" />, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/2/55206bce678ac0394d97dc04dd72398df2bdf572.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{E}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"26\" height=\"24\" />. - mathleticguyyy\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that the common ratio is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/d/1adaf592745a4acff59781990751af46ca5fe149.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\cos{x}}{\\sin{x}} = \\cot{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"105\" height=\"34\" />. This implies that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/3/2f3a2b21715f1250dc9e7b31ca0815cc1aa3097c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cot{x} \\cdot \\cos{x} = \\tan{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"154\" height=\"13\" />. This means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/4/b44f14437c88568214167dfaed43c44b81e6b727.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos{x} = \\frac{\\tan{x}}{\\cot{x}} = \\frac{sin^2{x}}{cos^2{x}} = \\frac{1- \\cos^2{x}}{\\cos^2{x}} = \\frac{1}{\\cos^2{x}}-1 \\implies \\cos^3{x} = 1 - \\cos^2{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"584\" height=\"41\" />. This was a lot of algebra, so take a second to convince yourself that it's all accurate. \n</p><p>Next, notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/0/e30a771517de6d31dd8ab0bd73447577533c1fc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_4 = \\tan{x} \\cdot \\cot{x} = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"167\" height=\"17\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/c/0fcc505cde0cdec319c14b8732ed843cb3adf505.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{4+i} = \\cot^{i}{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"101\" height=\"21\" /> by induction. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/4/5847a1f4999f913c6000f0b4ac4e1ed90c235186.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_6 = \\cot^2{x} = \\frac{\\cos^2{x}}{\\sin^2{x}} = \\frac{\\cos^2{x}}{1-\\cos^2{x}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"266\" height=\"42\" />. Substitute our value for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/e/2fe6bb2af1a0fd09ebc19b41fe9895a439f908ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 - \\cos^2{x} = \\cos^3{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"148\" height=\"18\" /> to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/5/005a519d6cec24058f94b708aed2c475e72d215f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cot^2{x} = \\sec{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"108\" height=\"17\" />. \n</p><p>From here, look back at our derivation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/9/9a90899644cfcb32c86247f0cf223d9bfd3b3e7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos^3{x} = 1 - \\cos^2{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"148\" height=\"18\" />. Rearrange to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/a/0aae17ab8f85919ad8209b765b9b6bb839161413.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos^2{x} \\left( \\cos{x}+1 \\right) = 1 \\implies  1+\\cos{x} = \\sec^2{x} = \\cot^4{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"423\" height=\"21\" /> by our second derivation. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/2/522ee082b06343f806de198a16408cc2245a8740.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$cot^4{x} = a_8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"84\" height=\"20\" /> which we showed with elementary induction that is left as an exercise for the reader, and our final answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/2/55206bce678ac0394d97dc04dd72398df2bdf572.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{E}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"26\" height=\"24\" />\n</p><p>- SumDumNerd\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B\" title=\"2010 AMC 12B\">2010 AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2010 AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2010 AMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2010 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 19\">Problem 19</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2010 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 21\">Problem 21</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2010 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2010 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2010 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2010 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2010 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2010 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2010 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2010 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2010 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2010 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2010 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2010 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2010 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2010 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2010 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2010 A